{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>One who strikes a man.</b> The reason this is mentioned after the law of the slave and the maidservant is that it is necessary to explain the law of one who strikes his slave or his maidservant, and this \"man\" is an Israelite." "<b>Shall surely be put to death.</b> Every case of מות יומת depends on the court, except for one, as you will see shortly."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:46.691253430Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}